WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.661
Why your back hurts in space, and the
simple move that eases it.

2
00:00:05.911 --> 00:00:10.118
In his first week on board, Rafael wakes
up with a sore lower back.

3
00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:15.667
He's not alone. About half of all
astronauts feel this in their first days.

4
00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.361
Without gravity pressing down,

5
00:00:18.361 --> 00:00:21.770
the discs between your vertebrae soak up
fluid and swell.

6
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.823
Your spine stretches, and you can grow up
to five centimeters taller.

7
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:29.555
The muscles and ligaments around it
complain.

8
00:00:30.455 --> 00:00:32.228
The move many astronauts use:

9
00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:35.836
pull your knees to your chest, and hold
for thirty seconds.

10
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:37.124
Breathe slowly.

11
00:00:38.024 --> 00:00:40.233
Sleep with your knees slightly bent,

12
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:44.527
and keep up your daily exercise,
especially on the resistance machine.

13
00:00:45.427 --> 00:00:50.115
If the pain shoots down a leg, or you feel
numbness or weakness, tell Keiko.

14
00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:54.452
Most of the time, the pain fades as your
body adapts.

15
00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:59.190
Back on Earth, go easy on heavy lifting at
first, while your spine readjusts.

